Below are 30 numbered crops from photos of indoor rooms. In each crop one object is outlined in green. Name the outlined object only.
For each crop give:
- "phrases": five different noun phrases a person might use for the outlined object, most likely first (for example "office chair", "desk chair", "swivel chair", "chair", "rolling chair");
- "question_noun": the single noun phrase a person writing a question about this room would most likely use for it;
- "part_of_larger": true if the outline covers only a part of a larger object (for example a drawer of a cabinet or a door of a wardrobe), else false;
- "one_object": true if the outline covers exactly one physical object, false if it covers several objects or none.
Reply with one JSON object and nothing else: {"1": {"phrases": [...], "question_noun": "...", "part_of_larger": false, "one_object": true}, ..., "30": {...}}

